OL,3,GNEWSA'Apocalyptic' fly-tip to stay
OL,4,Auntil fix found
OL,5,
OL,6,FFly-tipped waste dumped and described
OL,7,Fas "almost apocalyptic" will not be
OL,8,Ffully cleared until a long-term
OL,9,Fsolution is found to stop rubbish
OL,10,Frepeatedly returning.
OL,12,FBuilders' rubble, garden waste, kitchen
OL,13,Fappliances and office furniture line
OL,14,FOfferton Lane, just outside Worcester,
OL,15,Fwhere rubbish has built up over several
OL,16,Fyears.
OL,18,FCouncillor Sarah Murray, who represents
OL,19,Fthe St. Nicholas ward on Worcester City
OL,20,FCouncil, said previous clean-ups had
OL,21,Fproved ineffective because the site
OL,22,Fcontinued to attract fly-tipping.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,356,350,200,160,0,100
